From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "PCI: qcom: Power down PHY via PARF_PHY_CTRL before disabling rails/clocks"

This reverts upstream commit 8a847d3e9e5f1700beb5a0196e682f71837dfe5c.

On SM8550 (AYN Odin 2 Portal, WCN7850 on pcie0) the WCN7850 link never
leaves LTSSM Detect on Linux 7.2-rc7: every boot ends with "Device not
found" from dw_pcie_wait_for_link() and ath12k never probes. The same
device tree, firmware, and endpoint enumerate at Gen2 x2 on Linux 7.1.5.

The reverted commit makes qcom_pcie_deinit_2_7_0() assert
PARF_PHY_CTRL.PHY_TEST_PWR_DOWN before disabling clocks and regulators.
That deinit path is not suspend-only: it runs on every host-init
EPROBE_DEFER unwind during boot (the pwrctrl power-on flow defers about a
dozen times while the WCN power sequencer binds), so the wrapper PHY is
put into test power-down before the first real link-training attempt ever
happens. The subsequent init clears the bit again, in the documented
order, but the link still never trains: the endpoint is powered and holds
CLKREQ# asserted while the RC side stays in Detect. A clean post-boot
suspend/resume cycle (one deinit/init pass, no probe deferrals) fails the
same way.

This commit is the prime suspect but not yet proven: it is the only
behavioral boot-path change in pcie-qcom.c between the two kernels.
Revert the whole commit to A/B the regression on hardware; drop this if
the link still fails to train without it.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* Force PHY out of lowest power state */
+	/* enable PCIe clocks and resets */
 	val = readl(pcie->parf + PARF_PHY_CTRL);
 	val &= ~PHY_TEST_PWR_DOWN;
 	writel(val, pcie->parf + PARF_PHY_CTRL);
@@ -702,12 +702,6 @@
 static void qcom_pcie_deinit_2_3_2(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 {
 	struct qcom_pcie_resources_2_3_2 *res = &pcie->res.v2_3_2;
-	u32 val;
-
-	/* Force PHY to lowest power state*/
-	val = readl(pcie->parf + PARF_PHY_CTRL);
-	val |= PHY_TEST_PWR_DOWN;
-	writel(val, pcie->parf + PARF_PHY_CTRL);
 
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(res->num_clks, res->clks);
 	regulator_bulk_disable(ARRAY_SIZE(res->supplies), res->supplies);
@@ -740,7 +734,7 @@
